Enhancement: cold storage support (hot/cold repositories and warm-up)

Vaultic now supports cold-storage backends such as S3 Glacier or OVH Cold
Archive, in two complementary ways (mirroring rustic):

Hot/cold repositories split a repository over a cold location (all data packs;
a complete repository on its own) and a hot location (all metadata plus the
tree packs), so normal operations never touch the cold storage. Set it up with
`--repo-hot` and `init --hot-only`; the new `check --check-hot-cold` verifies
that both parts agree.

To read data packs from cold storage, vaultic runs a user-supplied warm-up
program: `--warm-up-command` (with `%id`/`%path`/`%ids`/`%paths` substitution),
`--warm-up-batch`, `--warm-up-wait` and `--warm-up-wait-command` (env
`VAULTIC_WARM_UP_*`). The program can report progress as JSON Lines
(`{"type":"pack-progress","warm":N}`). Warm-up runs before `restore`, `check`
and `prune` reads.

Both parts stay fully compatible with restic and rustic: the cold part is a
normal repository they can read, and the hot part is correctly recognized as a
hot repository by rustic.

